#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""RGB Controller: Qt front end for the rgb-controller daemon.

Closing the window hides it to the tray; the daemon is a separate (systemd user) service and
keeps switching profiles whether this window exists or not. Quit the GUI from the tray menu.

    rgb-controller-gui            open the window
    rgb-controller-gui --tray     start hidden in the tray (what the autostart entry uses)

Needs PySide6 (Arch: `pacman -S pyside6`). Everything here is event driven too: the GUI never
polls, the daemon pushes StateChanged / Log signals over D-Bus.

Look & feel: no stylesheets anywhere. Every colour comes from the active QPalette (so Breeze,
Breeze Dark and any custom KDE colour scheme just work), every icon comes from the icon theme.
"""

